# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile reads exactly ONE file from the context: docker_selfcheck.py,
# the build-time proof. Everything else the image contains -- the model code,
# the studio itself and the ~10.5 GB of weights -- is fetched over the network
# during the build (the studio is cloned from
# github.com/camenduru/TostAI-Sound-Effect-Studio).
#
# So: keep the build-time proof and drop everything else, which is either a
# local artifact or a copy of something the build downloads anyway.
#
# .env is the entry that would actually MATTER. It can hold HF_TOKEN, and the
# build context is uploaded to whatever builder is in use unless it is excluded
# here. A secret does not need to be in the context to be usable --
# `--secret ...,env=` reads it from the CALLER's environment instead. BuildKit
# warns when a secret is passed as ARG or ENV; it cannot warn about a file you
# forgot to ignore.
.env
.env.*

# The virtualenv is the one that would actually hurt: this checkout layers the
# model venv under .venv/ for local runs, and BuildKit would have to hash and
# transfer every file of it on every build. The image builds its own venv.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/

# Local audio the app wrote while being developed.
*.wav
*.pcm
outputs/
!outputs/.gitkeep

# The studio's own source. It comes from the git clone, not the context, so
# uploading it here would only slow the build down.
server.py
smoke_generate.py
docker-entrypoint.sh
static/
requirements.txt

# Not read at runtime; the README is documentation for the host checkout.
README.md

.git/
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
